MicroHOT 微熱

MicroHOT is a new, independent codebase inspired by AIHOT (https://github.com/KKKKhazix/AIHOT).
It is not affiliated with AIHOT and does not use AIHOT's name or logo.

The following parts are adapted from AIHOT:

- prompts/triage.md: translated and condensed from AIHOT's selection rubric
  (industry/prompts/selection-score.md) and pre-screen (industry/prompts/prefilter.md),
  including the five scoring axes and the per-type weights in src/microhot/triage.py.
- prompts/write.md: translated and adapted from AIHOT's writing prompts
  (industry/prompts/summarize-article.md, rules-answer-first-summary.md,
  rules-self-contained-title.md, rules-anti-hallucination.md, rules-domain.md, safety.md).
- prompts/digest.md: translated and condensed from AIHOT's story overview prompt
  (industry/prompts/story-digest.md).
- prompts/review.md: translated and condensed from AIHOT's period report prompt
  (industry/prompts/report-period.md).
- The heat formula (each independent source counted once within 48 hours, halving every
  24 hours), the rule-built daily edition, and the starter AI sources in config/sources.toml.
- Ideas reimplemented in Python: the hot-list badges and their thresholds (surge, new,
  rising; packages/backend/src/events/hot.ts), follow-ups in the daily edition, and measuring
  selection against human labels (SelectBench, packages/backend/src/admin/selectbench.ts).

